Today I learned about making directories in linux, directory is called a folder in window.

There are many ways to create directory in linux, like using linux command line to make it or making it using File Syatem

The way I use is command line using the following command line:

mkdir = This is a command line function used to create directories in linux

Syntaxs:

1. To create a single directory
mkdir /directory_name

2. To create a Multiple directories at once
mkdir d1 d2 d3

3. To create directory inside a directory in one line command
mkdir d1/d2/d3 = here d3 is inside d2 and d2 is inside d1

4. To create multiple directory inside a directory in one line command
mkdir d1/{d2/d3,d4/d5,d6/d7}  = here the tree is like d1 has d2, d4 and d6 inside of it and d3 is inside d2, d5 is inside d4 and d7 is inside d6


This is mkdir to you [mk-make dir-directory]
